VPNRouter bundles the Mullvad "win-split-tunnel" kernel driver
(mullvad-split-tunnel.sys / .cat / .inf) to provide OS-level per-app split
tunneling on Windows (exclude mode). The driver is used only when the user
enables exclude-mode routing; its absence disables the feature (VPNRouter
falls back to sing-box process_name routing).

Source (driver):  https://github.com/mullvad/win-split-tunnel
Signed binaries:  https://github.com/mullvad/mullvadvpn-app-binaries
                  @ cc0affb2f06e870fb594e2dd6d61049611991586
                  x86_64-pc-windows-msvc/split-tunnel/

The driver is distributed by Mullvad VPN AB under a dual
GPL-3.0-or-later / MPL-2.0 license. The .sys is Authenticode-signed by
"CN=Mullvad VPN AB" and carries a Microsoft Windows Hardware Compatibility
Publisher attestation countersignature (so it loads on production Win10/11
x64 without test-signing).

VPNRouter neither modifies nor relinks the driver: it is bundled verbatim
(sha256-pinned) and driven over its public IOCTL interface. See the upstream
repositories above for the full license texts and source code.
